      "author_login": "DekoMoon",
      "content": "Not able to reproduce this anymore on my Ubuntu machine (but still reproducible on my Windows 11 machine), but did anyone else encounter this error in the requirements.txt installation step?\n\nI tried to install each of the package in requirements.txt individually, and the one that caused the error seems to be `flash_attn>=2.7.4.post1`.\n\nSome things I noticed while I was testing on my Windows machine:\n\n*  After failing to run `pip install -r requirements.txt` due to `torch` not being found when installing `flash_attn`, I ran `python`, then ran `import torch`, and received the same error message `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'torch'`. it seems like `flash_attn` is being run first in requirements.txt?\n    ```\n      torch>=2.6.0\n      flash_attn>=2.7.4.post1\n      tokenizers>=0.21.1\n      numpy>=2.1.0\n      rich\n      typing_extensions\n      safetensors>=0.3.2\n      ninja\n    ```\n\n* I also tried to install torch before running `pip install -r requirements.txt` with the following command `pip install torch>=2.6.0` and it seem'd to have installed the cpu version of torch when I ran the following in python:\n    ```python\n    import torch\n    torch.__version__\n    ```\n    * Not sure if it was supposed to use cpu or gpu, but the cpu torch failed with \n        ```\n        OSError: CUDA_HOME environment variable is not set. Please set it to your CUDA install root.\n        torch.__version__  = 2.6.0+cpu\n        ```\n    * so I ended up installing cuda torch:\n        ```sh\n        pip install torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu124\n        ```\n    * Running `pip install flas_attn>=2.7.4.post1` now hangs at the building wheels step in Windows 11.",
